OL,3,GNEWSAThe giant pre-historic insect
OL,4,Afound by miners
OL,5,
OL,6,FBefore dinosaurs roamed the Earth,
OL,7,Fseagull-sized dragonfly-like insects
OL,8,Fknown as griffinflies ruled the skies.
OL,10,FMore than 300 million years later,
OL,11,Fminers unearthed two fossilised remains
OL,12,Fof the "gigantic" insects 500m
OL,13,F(1,640ft) below the surface at Bolsover
OL,14,FColliery, in Derbyshire, in 1979.
OL,16,FThe only known remains of whalleyala
OL,17,Fbolsoveri, with a 17.4cm wingspan, and
OL,18,Farctotypus diluculum, believed to have
OL,19,Fhad a wingspan of about 50cm, were
OL,20,Fdiscovered and are now housed at
OL,21,FLondon's Natural History Museum.
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,363,360,200,160,0,100
